      "content": "#include <algorithm>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <utility>\n#include <vector>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nstatic const long long MOD = 1000000007LL;\n\nlong long mod_pow(long long base, long long exponent) {\n    long long result = 1;\n    while (exponent > 0) {\n        if (exponent & 1) result = result * base % MOD;\n        base = base * base % MOD;\n        exponent >>= 1;\n    }\n    return result;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    int n, m;\n    if (!(cin >> n >> m)) return 0;\n\n    vector<pair<int, int>> blocked;\n    blocked.reserve(m);\n    bool blocked_start = false;\n    for (int i = 0; i < m; ++i) {\n        int y, x;\n        cin >> y >> x;\n        if (y == 0 && x == 0) blocked_start = true;\n        blocked.emplace_back(y, x);\n    }\n\n    if (blocked_start) {\n        cout << 0 << '\\n';\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    sort(blocked.begin(), blocked.end());\n    blocked.erase(unique(blocked.begin(), blocked.end()), blocked.end());\n    blocked.erase(remove(blocked.begin(), blocked.end(), make_pair(n - 1, n - 1)), blocked.end());\n    blocked.emplace_back(n - 1, n - 1);\n\n    const int max_factorial = 2 * (n - 1);\n    vector<long long> factorial(max_factorial + 1), inverse_factorial(max_factorial + 1);\n    factorial[0] = 1;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= max_factorial; ++i)\n        factorial[i] = factorial[i - 1] * i % MOD;\n    inverse_factorial[max_factorial] = mod_pow(factorial[max_factorial], MOD - 2);\n    for (int i = max_factorial; i > 0; --i)\n        inverse_factorial[i - 1] = inverse_factorial[i] * i % MOD;\n\n    auto choose = [&](int total, int selected) -> long long {\n        if (selected < 0 || selected > total) return 0;\n        return factorial[total] * inverse_factorial[selected] % MOD *\n               inverse_factorial[total - selected] % MOD;\n    };\n\n    vector<long long> ways(blocked.size());\n    for (size_t i = 0; i < blocked.size(); ++i) {\n        int y = blocked[i].first;\n        int x = blocked[i].second;\n        ways[i] = choose(y + x, y);\n        for (size_t j = 0; j < i; ++j) {\n            int py = blocked[j].first;\n            int px = blocked[j].second;\n            if (py <= y && px <= x)\n                ways[i] = (ways[i] - ways[j] * choose(y - py + x - px, y - py) % MOD + MOD) % MOD;\n        }\n    }\n\n    cout << ways.back() << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Sparse-obstacle inclusion-exclusion reduces the grid DP's quadratic dependence on N to work based on the number of unique blocked cells, while preserving exact modulo results for every valid grid and obstacle arrangement.",
  "notes": "This is a bounded algorithmic alternative to row-wise OpenMP work sharing: the DP has a true left-to-right dependency within each row and a row-to-row dependency, so straightforward parallel-for directives would be incorrect or add synchronization overhead. No OpenMP transformation is claimed.",
